{"@context":"https://schema.org","@id":"https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/teriyaki-salmon-parcels#Recipe","@type":"Recipe","description":"These easy steamed fish parcels with Japanese seasoning are an ideal way to get kids in the kitchen","image":{"@type":"ImageObject","height":574,"width":768,"url":"https://images.immediate.co.uk/production/volatile/sites/30/2020/08/salmon_9-8ec47b9.jpg?resize=768,574"},"mainEntityOfPage":{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/teriyaki-salmon-parcels"},"name":"Teriyaki salmon parcels","url":"https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/teriyaki-salmon-parcels","author":[{"@type":"Person","name":"Barney Desmazery","url":"https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/author/barneydesmazery"}],"dateModified":"2024-11-23T20:05:09+00:00","datePublished":"2022-12-18T11:26:36+00:00","headline":"Teriyaki salmon parcels","keywords":"30-60 minutes, 400 kcal or less, Barney Desmazery, Cooking with kids, Family friendly, Fish parcels, healthy salmon recipe, Kids cooking, low-calorie fish recipes, Omega 3, Steamed fish","publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Good Food","url":"https://www.bbcgoodfood.com","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","height":65,"url":"https://images.immediate.co.uk/production/volatile/sites/30/2024/03/cropped-GF-new-teal-1-7004649-a80b70d.png?resize=265,65","width":265}},"isAccessibleForFree":"False","hasPart":{"@type":"WebPageElement","isAccessibleForFree":"False","cssSelector":".js-piano-locked-content"},"cookTime":"PT20M","nutrition":{"@type":"NutritionInformation","calories":"257 calories","fatContent":"13 grams fat","saturatedFatContent":"2 grams saturated fat","carbohydrateContent":"8 grams carbohydrates","sugarContent":"6 grams sugar","fiberContent":"3 grams fiber","proteinContent":"25 grams protein","sodiumContent":"0.8 milligram of sodium"},"prepTime":"PT15M","recipeCategory":"Main course","recipeCuisine":"Japanese","recipeIngredient":["2 tbsp low-salt soy sauce","1 tbsp clear honey","1 garlic clove finely chopped","1 tbsp mirin (optional)","a little sunflower oil","300g long-stem broccoli","4 x 100g salmon fillets","1 small piece of ginger cut into matchsticks","a little sesame oil (optional)","sliced spring onions toasted sesame seeds and cooked rice, to serve"],"recipeInstructions":[{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"KIDS: The writing in bold is for you. ADULTS: The rest is for you. Make the sauce and marinade. In a small bowl, whisk together the soy, honey, garlic and mirin and set aside."},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Cut out some squares of foil. Using scissors, cut out 4 squares of foil, each about 30cm square. Brush each piece of foil with a little oil and bring the edges of the foil up a little."},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Fill your parcels. Place a couple of broccoli stems on each one, then sit a salmon fillet on top and scatter over the ginger."},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Spoon over the sauce. Spoon the sauce over each salmon fillet and drizzle with a little sesame oil, if you like."},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Close the parcels. Fold over the edges of the foil together to seal and place the parcels on a baking sheet. Can be prepared up to 1 day ahead."},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Cook the parcels. Heat oven to 200C/180C fan/gas 6. Get your child to place the parcels in the oven for 15-20 mins, but ensure an adult removes them, then leave to stand for a few mins. Serve each parcel on a plate and let each person open it themselves. Serve with spring onions and sesame seeds for scattering over, and some rice on the side."}],"recipeYield":4,"totalTime":"PT35M"}